       of structures, each describing a segment or other information the  sys‐
       tem needs to prepare the program for execution.  An object file _s_e_g_m_e_n_t
       contains one or more _s_e_c_t_i_o_n_s.  Program headers are meaningful only for
       executable  and  shared object files.  A file specifies its own program
       header size with the ELF header’s _e___p_h_e_n_t_s_i_z_e and _e___p_h_n_u_m members.  The
       ELF program header is described by the type  _E_l_f_3_2___P_h_d_r  or  _E_l_f_6_4___P_h_d_r
       depending on the architecture:

           typedef struct {
               uint32_t   p_type;
               Elf32_Off  p_offset;
               Elf32_Addr p_vaddr;
               Elf32_Addr p_paddr;
               uint32_t   p_filesz;
               uint32_t   p_memsz;
               uint32_t   p_flags;
               uint32_t   p_align;
